+## 1. State-Specific Retrieval Canonicalization
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Extend the pure retrieval canonicalization path to recognize only supported, explicitly stated ball-valve phrases for an installed electric actuator versus an actuator-ready valve, emit at most one distinct alternate query, and verify focused unit tests cover each state.
+- [ ] 1.2 Ensure each alternate retains the source product, DN, PN, material, joining, designation, and explicit execution terms while adding only catalog-native vocabulary for the same recognised control state; verify focused tests assert retained and added terms.
+- [ ] 1.3 Preserve the existing no-op behavior for a generic drive, standalone actuator product, ambiguous electrical wording, unsupported product anchors, and queries without explicit actuator state; verify focused negative tests assert no state-specific catalog term is injected.
+
+## 2. Hybrid-Path Regression Coverage
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Verify the matcher continues to send the normalized original tender text to reranking, result output, and duplicate-query caching when the new alternate exists; add or update a focused mocked matcher test.
+- [ ] 2.2 Verify existing hybrid retrieval behavior still retrieves the original query first, merges a state-alternate result by LD id without duplicate modality credit, and keeps original candidates when alternate retrieval fails; add focused mocked retriever regressions only where current coverage does not exercise the new canonical representation.
+
+## 3. Verification
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Run `python -m pytest -q` and resolve product-code test failures without editing GOLD, harness, holdout, or supervisor-evaluation artifacts.

